WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — mei (60s) Narrator Nylo

1
00:00:00.475 --> 00:00:05.559
Biological cells throttle non-essential work when ATP drops;

2
00:00:05.559 --> 00:00:10.729
conventional computers run full tilt until voltage collapses.

3
00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:18.273
Whether running on a coin cell or following renewable curtailment in a megawatt campus,

4
00:00:18.273 --> 00:00:20.770
tasks request a joule hold first.

5
00:00:21.732 --> 00:00:27.356
Across 10,000 simulated cold-chain wakeups at minus 20 Celsius,

6
00:00:27.356 --> 00:00:32.712
metabolic shedding preserves 100 percent of critical alerts.

7
00:00:33.674 --> 00:00:39.082
Zero DRC violations across 2-layer KiCad Gerbers,

8
00:00:39.082 --> 00:00:46.586
paired with a 3D B-Rep enclosure and 2,680 signed det-CBOR receipts.

9
00:00:47.548 --> 00:00:54.793
Every table distinguishes emulator instruction counts and datasheet schedules from physical bench power.
